1
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,480
You'll tell me everything

2
00:02:40,560 --> 00:02:42,360
from now on.

3
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:44,280
Starting with your treatment plan.

4
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,160
I have Thamrong.

5
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:48,360
You have me too, Dad,

6
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,000
in case you've forgotten.

7
00:02:50,080 --> 00:02:51,280
Korn.

8
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,520
Go with Grandfather.

9
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:53,920
Rawee can drive me.

10
00:02:54,680 --> 00:02:55,520
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I don't know.</font></font></i>

11
00:02:56,200 --> 00:02:58,760
Maybe I'm getting tired of all this.

12
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:00,680
If you've had enough,

13
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:03,440
you can always tell me.

14
00:03:03,520 --> 00:03:05,280
I'll sort it out for you.

15
00:03:05,360 --> 00:03:07,040
I found this document.

16
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,040
You're not Nada's son.

17
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:14,760
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You have to vouch for me.</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Say you were with me in my office.</font></font></i>

18
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,760
You have to help me before anyone else.

19
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:20,040
I think you've known for a long time

20
00:03:20,120 --> 00:03:22,000
that I'm not your biological son.

21
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:24,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But what's even stranger</font></font></i>

22
00:03:24,160 --> 00:03:26,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">is why the results show you and Wee</font></font></i>

23
00:03:26,240 --> 00:03:27,800
aren't mother and son.

24
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Are you sure</font></font></i>

25
00:03:37,280 --> 00:03:40,440
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">you were the first to find Mr. Prajak,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">not your brother?</font></font></i>

26
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:42,400
I don't know.

27
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:44,920
And I don't understand

28
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:46,840
why you care so much about this.

29
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:50,800
Have you ever asked Korn
these questions to his face?

30
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:53,880
Who knows?

31
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:57,120
Mr. Prajak might already have
Ms. Pimpa's DNA test results.

32
00:03:57,840 --> 00:04:00,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Was there anything unusual</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">in Aunt Pim's room?</font></font></i>

33
00:04:00,160 --> 00:04:01,760
What do you mean?

34
00:04:02,400 --> 00:04:06,680
Well, documents or anything like that.

35
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:08,560
No.

36
00:04:09,160 --> 00:04:11,480
He just offered me a job as an assistant.

37
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:14,440
An assistant?

38
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:17,000
Whose assistant? His assistant?

39
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,040
Yeah.

40
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,800
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You said you were tired</font></font></i>

41
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:26,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and uneasy and wanted</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">to come clean and come home.</font></font></i>

42
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:32,440
I've changed my mind. I want to help
Ms. Nada to repay her kindness.

43
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:37,680
Sorry you got close to Grandfather
for nothing, Wee.

44
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,640
Mom.

45
00:05:08,960 --> 00:05:10,320
What are you doing here?

46
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:14,360
What's wrong with him?
What did you do to him, Korn?

47
00:05:15,760 --> 00:05:16,720
Come with me first.

48
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,640
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You have to vouch for me.</font></font></i>

49
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:25,720
Say you were with me in my office
and I hadn't been to Mr. Prajak's office.

50
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,960
Was that Ms. Nada's father?

51
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,680
What's wrong with him?

52
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,200
What did you do, Korn?

53
00:05:31,280 --> 00:05:32,520
Mom!

54
00:05:32,600 --> 00:05:34,280
Stay calm.

55
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:37,600
We just had an argument.

56
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,120
It was all an accident.

57
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:42,960
I'm about to take you to meet Grandfather.

58
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:46,640
You don't know anything
about what happened in that room.

59
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,920
Wee is his real grandson.

60
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,880
He'll help Wee no matter what.

61
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,640
Besides, Wee didn't hurt Grandfather.

62
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:58,520
What could anyone blame him for?

63
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:03,880
I'm your son, Mom.

64
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,120
Wee isn't.

65
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,600
He's already safe.

66
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,400
You have to help me before anyone else.

67
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:31,160
Oh.

68
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,760
Why are you sitting here in the dark?

69
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,880
I couldn't sleep.

70
00:06:35,960 --> 00:06:37,720
I have a bad feeling.

71
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,760
I wonder how Mr. Prajak is doing.

72
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:41,560
Is that all?

73
00:06:47,280 --> 00:06:49,600
Do you know something I don't, Mom?

74
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:54,680
Well, nothing. We were together all day.

75
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:58,760
Good.

76
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:03,320
I hope we're not worried
about the same thing, Mom.

77
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:16,440
I thought you'd stay over there.

78
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:18,280
What is it?

79
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:22,600
I'd like to talk to you, Mother.

80
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:30,560
Aunt Pim secretly had our blood
tested for DNA.

81
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:41,600
And I think you've known for a long time

82
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:44,080
that I'm not your biological son.

83
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,480
But what's even stranger

84
00:07:48,680 --> 00:07:50,880
is why the results show you and Wee

85
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:53,320
aren't mother and son.

86
00:08:05,560 --> 00:08:06,800
Who are you really?

87
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,040
But you don't have to answer me.

88
00:08:14,320 --> 00:08:15,440
What do you want?

89
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:19,240
Legally adopt me.

90
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:21,880
Then we won't need a DNA test
that could expose us.

91
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,080
I promise

92
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,320
this will stay between us

93
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:30,360
forever.

94
00:08:33,919 --> 00:08:34,840
And one more thing.

95
00:08:35,520 --> 00:08:38,120
You should get it done
as soon as possible.

96
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:40,360
Because once Grandfather wakes up,

97
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:42,960
I'm not going down alone.

98
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:46,040
You're the one who did this

99
00:08:46,880 --> 00:08:48,320
to my father, aren't you?

100
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:53,600
Are you sure he's your father?

101
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,520
Get the documents ready.

102
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,600
We'll take care of it tomorrow.

103
00:09:01,280 --> 00:09:02,440
Thank you.

104
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,600
Mother.

105
00:09:20,520 --> 00:09:21,760
Rice porridge, dear.

106
00:09:21,840 --> 00:09:23,040
Thank you.

107
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,240
And here's some water.

108
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:29,040
Oh, Wee. Come sit down.
I'll get you some porridge.

109
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:43,800
What are you trying to get
out of my mom this time?

110
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:51,200
I'm not sure. Depends

111
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:52,880
on what else she lets slip.

112
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,920
Hey.

113
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,160
Relax.

114
00:09:56,080 --> 00:09:59,160
All I got was her porridge recipe.
It smells so good.

115
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:06,840
Why do you think

116
00:10:06,920 --> 00:10:09,560
what happened to Mr. Prajak
has something to do with Korn?

117
00:10:12,600 --> 00:10:15,440
Because I took your mother
to Korn's office myself.

118
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,880
That's how I know Korn wasn't there.

119
00:10:17,960 --> 00:10:19,560
And no one can confirm

120
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:22,080
where he was when it happened.

121
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,560
Do you…

122
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:31,480
have anything you'd like to confess?

123
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,320
I love you.

124
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:43,600
What?

125
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,440
Is that

126
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,000
what you wanted me to confess?

127
00:10:58,640 --> 00:10:59,520
Here you go.

128
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:01,200
This one's yours, Wee.

129
00:11:01,280 --> 00:11:02,440
Thanks, Mom.

130
00:11:02,520 --> 00:11:04,680
I'll go get you some water.

131
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,320
This is yours.

132
00:11:58,520 --> 00:11:59,800
Where's mine?

133
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:32,640
Wait.

134
00:12:36,720 --> 00:12:38,560
What about our DNA test results?

135
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:42,000
Why would I keep evidence
that could be used against me?

136
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:44,360
I tore it to shreds a long time ago.

137
00:12:46,120 --> 00:12:48,240
Then from now on, we go our separate ways.

138
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,720
Stay out of my way.

139
00:12:50,800 --> 00:12:53,320
Don't come asking questions
or looking into anything.

140
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:55,840
Yes, Mother.

141
00:13:19,080 --> 00:13:20,080
Aunt Da.

142
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:22,080
Dad's worried about you.

143
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:25,840
He's afraid something like that
might happen again.

144
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:28,440
You should hire a bodyguard.

145
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:29,720
Oh.

146
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,760
There's no need to go that far, Alyssa.

147
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:35,360
I only go between home and work.

148
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:38,440
And my neighborhood is very secure.

149
00:13:38,520 --> 00:13:40,720
Besides, Phakorn is there with me.

150
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,360
I'm sure I'll be fine.

151
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:49,560
Ever since Phakorn came back from America
and moved in with you,

152
00:13:50,520 --> 00:13:51,800
it's been one thing after another.

153
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,360
Aunt Da.

154
00:13:58,400 --> 00:14:00,800
Don't trust the people
around you completely.

155
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,400
I'm worried about you.

156
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:08,080
Thank you and your dad, Alyssa.

157
00:14:08,840 --> 00:14:09,840
I'll be more careful

158
00:14:10,440 --> 00:14:12,080
from now on.

159
00:14:15,800 --> 00:14:17,160
Okay.

160
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,160
Ms. Nada.

161
00:14:21,640 --> 00:14:22,760
The doctor would like to see you.

162
00:14:23,440 --> 00:14:24,600
Thank you.

163
00:14:25,760 --> 00:14:27,360
I'll go talk to the doctor first.

164
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,600
Are you leaving now, Ms. Alyssa?

165
00:14:45,520 --> 00:14:47,120
We keep running into each other.

166
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:49,200
Every time we've met,

167
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:51,040
it's been a coincidence.

168
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:55,160
So breakfast at my house this morning
was a coincidence too?

169
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:00,720
You really don't seem to trust Korn.

170
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,880
Your brother hasn't exactly given me
a reason to trust him.

171
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,480
I don't see
what's so suspicious about Korn.

172
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:16,560
The DNA results are out.
You know that, don't you?

173
00:15:16,640 --> 00:15:18,120
Really?

174
00:15:18,200 --> 00:15:20,080
Then where are the DNA results?

175
00:15:20,840 --> 00:15:24,040
Maybe Ms. Pimpa has them
and already sent them to Mr. Prajak.

176
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:27,240
You can't just throw accusations around
like that, Ms. Alyssa.

177
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:29,880
If you have evidence, show me.

178
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:32,800
Lay it all out,
and I'll address it all at once.

179
00:15:34,240 --> 00:15:36,640
I forgot I'm talking to Phakorn's lawyer.

180
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,080
Deny everything and call it fair.

181
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:40,800
I never said I was fair.

182
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,880
I just know Korn much better than you do.

183
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,440
Are you sure

184
00:15:47,240 --> 00:15:50,440
the Phakorn you know
is still the same person?

185
00:15:55,400 --> 00:15:58,560
Actually, I like seeing you
defend your brother.

186
00:15:59,520 --> 00:16:01,000
You really go all out for him.

187
00:16:02,240 --> 00:16:04,080
So I'd like to offer you a job.

188
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:06,920
I don't take side jobs.

189
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,800
It's only short-term.

190
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,680
Tell me what it is first.

191
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,720
Help me with the sale agreement
for Tawan Island.

192
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,640
Find someone else.

193
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:24,680
If you agree,

194
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:29,040
I'll tell you one of Phakorn's secrets.

195
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:33,560
You're the most devious woman
I've ever met.

196
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,320
So?

197
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,280
Do we have a deal?

198
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:42,040
Fine. Deal.

199
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,760
If you promise me

200
00:16:44,840 --> 00:16:47,600
you'll sort things out
properly between you and Phakorn.

201
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,280
If you love Korn,
just say yes and settle it.

202
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:54,440
Don't make his last name a condition.

203
00:16:55,160 --> 00:16:58,480
But if you don't love him, tell him.

204
00:16:59,160 --> 00:17:00,520
My brother really likes you.

205
00:17:01,240 --> 00:17:03,240
I hope you'll be just as sincere with him.

206
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:07,960
After that whole speech,

207
00:17:08,040 --> 00:17:10,599
it still comes down
to what's best for your brother.

208
00:17:12,079 --> 00:17:14,839
I really should give you
a Brother of the Year award.

209
00:17:21,079 --> 00:17:23,160
Where is it? Hand it over.

210
00:17:29,920 --> 00:17:31,120
Alright.

211
00:17:32,880 --> 00:17:35,720
I'll sort things out with Korn soon.

212
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,280
And you'd

213
00:17:39,320 --> 00:17:40,800
better not back out.

214
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:17,640
Father collapsed because of you,
didn't he?

215
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:19,800
What are you talking about?

216
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:22,800
Don't think I don't know

217
00:18:23,480 --> 00:18:24,680
what you're planning.

218
00:18:26,080 --> 00:18:28,040
I just haven't said anything.

219
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:29,960
Really?

220
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,920
Then…

221
00:18:34,240 --> 00:18:36,080
Tell me what you think I'm planning.

222
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:40,840
You know

223
00:18:40,920 --> 00:18:44,240
Father has to rewrite his will
now that Pim is dead, don't you?

224
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,560
That's why you're upset, right?

225
00:18:47,480 --> 00:18:49,040
Why would I be upset?

226
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:52,720
What does Pim's death
have to do with the will?

227
00:18:53,280 --> 00:18:56,400
I'm practically
Father's representative already.

228
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:03,240
Must be hard not being the favorite child.

229
00:19:08,360 --> 00:19:10,080
And let me warn you.

230
00:19:10,160 --> 00:19:11,880
Stay away from my son.

231
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,240
Don't even think about using him.

232
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:21,800
Which son

233
00:19:23,120 --> 00:19:24,360
do you mean, Da?

234
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:21,720
Where are you going?

235
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,320
I'm having dinner with Alyssa.

236
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:28,200
Here's an update on Grandfather.

237
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:31,080
Try to look genuinely concerned.

238
00:20:33,280 --> 00:20:34,440
How is he?

239
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,120
Grandfather

240
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:40,600
is out of danger.

241
00:20:45,440 --> 00:20:47,120
But we still don't know

242
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:50,640
when he'll regain consciousness.

243
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:54,320
So he might not wake up?

244
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,640
Well, something like that.

245
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,840
But even if he regains consciousness,

246
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:09,600
there's still no telling

247
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,560
who caused

248
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:13,480
his collapse.

249
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:18,800
One more thing.

250
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:22,360
Stay away from Panas.

251
00:21:22,440 --> 00:21:25,920
He's not approaching you
because he means well.

252
00:21:29,280 --> 00:21:30,720
You don't have to worry about me.

253
00:21:30,800 --> 00:21:32,440
I can take care of myself.

254
00:21:34,040 --> 00:21:35,560
And keep your promise.

255
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,600
We stay out of each other's way.

256
00:21:47,360 --> 00:21:48,320
Of course.

257
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:51,520
We're in the same boat now.

258
00:21:52,200 --> 00:21:53,480
Mother.

259
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:04,840
Here.

260
00:22:05,920 --> 00:22:08,040
You should stay here
for the night, Mr. Nimit.

261
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:10,040
I'm feeling better.

262
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:13,280
Why should I stay here like I'm sick?

263
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:18,240
Are you sure, Mr. Nimit?

264
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:22,440
Yes. Come on, let's go home.

265
00:22:22,520 --> 00:22:23,760
Well…

266
00:22:23,840 --> 00:22:25,680
You don't want me to tell Ms. Alyssa?

267
00:22:28,120 --> 00:22:29,920
You promised her

268
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,560
you'd tell her everything.

269
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:36,480
No need. Alyssa's busy.

270
00:22:37,040 --> 00:22:39,240
She's working
between Bangkok and Chonburi.

271
00:22:39,320 --> 00:22:41,280
I don't want to disrupt her work.

272
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:43,840
And stop treating me

273
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,560
like I'm sick.

274
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:48,000
Alright.

275
00:23:08,040 --> 00:23:09,480
If you agree,

276
00:23:10,240 --> 00:23:12,880
I'll tell you one of Phakorn's secrets.

277
00:23:15,040 --> 00:23:18,400
You're the most devious woman
I've ever met.

278
00:23:18,480 --> 00:23:19,640
So?

279
00:23:20,680 --> 00:23:21,920
Do we have a deal?

280
00:23:22,680 --> 00:23:24,520
Fine. Deal.

281
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,520
If you promise me

282
00:23:27,600 --> 00:23:30,400
you'll sort things out
properly between you and Phakorn.

283
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:33,960
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">If you love Korn,</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">just say yes and settle it.</font></font></i>

284
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:37,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Don't make his last name a condition.</font></font></i>

285
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:40,760
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But if you don't love him, tell him.</font></font></i>

286
00:23:41,880 --> 00:23:43,040
My brother really likes you.

287
00:23:43,920 --> 00:23:45,800
I hope you'll be just as sincere with him.

288
00:23:48,720 --> 00:23:50,720
After that whole speech,

289
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:53,320
it still comes down
to what's best for your brother.

290
00:23:54,680 --> 00:23:57,560
I really should give you
a Brother of the Year award.

291
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:05,800
Where is it? Hand it over.

292
00:24:12,600 --> 00:24:13,760
Alright.

293
00:24:15,480 --> 00:24:18,280
I'll sort things out with Korn soon.

294
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:20,800
And you'd

295
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:23,440
better not back out.

296
00:25:29,960 --> 00:25:30,840
Please.

297
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:51,760
This reminds me of our first dinner
in America.

298
00:25:53,480 --> 00:25:55,480
Our first dinner?

299
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:58,360
Wasn't that your burnt basil stir-fry?

300
00:26:00,600 --> 00:26:01,600
That doesn't count.

301
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:07,320
By the way,
you've been pretty busy lately, right?

302
00:26:07,400 --> 00:26:08,960
We haven't seen much of each other.

303
00:26:10,720 --> 00:26:12,360
I've had a few things on my mind.

304
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:21,200
Work, for one.
And my father's been a little unwell.

305
00:26:34,480 --> 00:26:36,560
I got what you wanted.

306
00:26:37,600 --> 00:26:39,360
Can we be together now?

307
00:26:49,600 --> 00:26:52,120
MR. PHAKORN TAYAWAT

308
00:27:03,840 --> 00:27:04,840
Alyssa.

309
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:08,520
Alyssa.

310
00:27:12,360 --> 00:27:13,440
How did you get it?

311
00:27:14,520 --> 00:27:17,560
My ID card? I went to the district office.

312
00:27:19,480 --> 00:27:21,040
No.

313
00:27:23,320 --> 00:27:24,400
Oh.

314
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:26,760
You mean the Tayawat surname?

315
00:27:27,760 --> 00:27:31,360
It was mine from the start. You know that.

316
00:27:33,080 --> 00:27:35,600
If you love Korn,
just say yes and settle it.

317
00:27:36,280 --> 00:27:37,960
Don't make his last name a condition.

318
00:27:38,840 --> 00:27:42,080
But if you don't love him, tell him.

319
00:27:42,840 --> 00:27:44,240
My brother really likes you.

320
00:27:44,880 --> 00:27:46,760
I hope you'll be just as sincere with him.

321
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:05,280
Ask me again.

322
00:28:19,320 --> 00:28:20,720
Will you be my girlfriend?

323
00:28:31,360 --> 00:28:32,640
Yes.

324
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:14,560
Good morning, brother.

325
00:30:14,640 --> 00:30:16,640
I guess my order to stay on the island

326
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,240
means nothing now.

327
00:30:21,200 --> 00:30:22,800
Come on, brother.

328
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:26,240
That was years ago.

329
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,520
Haven't you missed your little brother?

330
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:31,400
What do you want?

331
00:30:34,000 --> 00:30:35,080
You're seriously ill, too.

332
00:30:35,160 --> 00:30:36,080
So?

333
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:39,600
Before anything happens to you,

334
00:30:40,160 --> 00:30:42,640
I want you to sort out the land.

335
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:44,160
What land?

336
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:47,960
The Tawan Island Resort
and the surrounding land.

337
00:30:49,320 --> 00:30:50,880
I want to expand the resort.

338
00:30:51,960 --> 00:30:53,360
Don't lie to me.

339
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:56,880
If you wanted to expand the resort,
you would've done it years ago.

340
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:58,240
Okay.

341
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:01,880
I'm going to sell the resort.
Someone wants to buy it.

342
00:31:02,840 --> 00:31:05,920
If I can get the land all the way
up to Ms. Nada's house, even better.

343
00:31:08,080 --> 00:31:09,560
But…

344
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:11,320
if your daughter refuses--

345
00:31:11,400 --> 00:31:12,680
Stay away from Alyssa!

346
00:31:16,040 --> 00:31:17,040
Nimit!

347
00:31:17,640 --> 00:31:20,120
Hey, don't you die on me!

348
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:22,840
Sort out the land first! Hey!

349
00:31:23,480 --> 00:31:24,520
Nimit!

350
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:27,240
Thamrong!

351
00:31:27,320 --> 00:31:29,640
Come check on your boss, Thamrong!

352
00:31:30,960 --> 00:31:32,080
Thamrong!

353
00:31:35,040 --> 00:31:36,040
Thamrong!

354
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:47,000
Yes, Mom?

355
00:31:48,600 --> 00:31:52,120
Mr. Nimit's in the hospital?
Is it serious?

356
00:31:54,280 --> 00:31:55,680
Which hospital?

357
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:03,080
-Oh! I forgot my keys.
-What is it, dear?

358
00:32:03,160 --> 00:32:04,920
Calm down.

359
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:06,760
Alyssa, calm down.

360
00:32:07,760 --> 00:32:11,480
Mom, I'll call you back.
Ms. Alyssa's right here.

361
00:32:17,360 --> 00:32:19,120
Can I help with anything?

362
00:32:24,440 --> 00:32:27,440
-WANT TO GO TO A CONCERT THIS SATURDAY?
-LET ME THINK ABOUT IT

363
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:18,920
PHAKORN

364
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:43,760
MORNING, STILL ASLEEP?
GENESIS GREEN ENERGY PLC

365
00:33:48,040 --> 00:33:49,560
Shit.

366
00:33:57,440 --> 00:34:00,040
GENESIS GREEN ENERGY PLC
TOTAL ESTIMATED DAMAGE: 40 MILLION

367
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:31,920
Choke on it.

368
00:34:43,239 --> 00:34:45,239
You're not dressed for work yet?

369
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:50,920
There's a project meeting today.

370
00:34:51,600 --> 00:34:52,920
Don't be late.

371
00:34:53,600 --> 00:34:55,239
We'll be discussing the budget too.

372
00:35:12,680 --> 00:35:13,880
How's Dad?

373
00:35:13,960 --> 00:35:15,240
He's in a patient room now.

374
00:35:16,160 --> 00:35:17,920
Good thing he didn't fall
and hit his head.

375
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:20,880
Otherwise, he'd end up bedridden
like Mr. Prajak too.

376
00:35:21,720 --> 00:35:22,560
Aunt Pat!

377
00:35:28,120 --> 00:35:30,440
What happened to him?

378
00:35:30,520 --> 00:35:33,560
How did he suddenly pass out
and end up in the hospital like this?

379
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:35,160
He argued with Mr. Jak.

380
00:35:35,760 --> 00:35:36,960
What about?

381
00:35:37,880 --> 00:35:39,080
The resort.

382
00:35:42,400 --> 00:35:43,360
Mrs. Walai.

383
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:46,960
Could you take Ms. Alyssa and Ms. Pat
to see Mr. Nimit in his room first?

384
00:35:47,040 --> 00:35:49,360
-Of course. Let's go.
-Alright.

385
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:00,600
Dad!

386
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:04,480
Sorry for all the trouble.

387
00:36:05,920 --> 00:36:08,320
Everyone's really worried about you.

388
00:36:08,400 --> 00:36:10,680
And of all days,
the driver had to be off today.

389
00:36:10,760 --> 00:36:13,120
Alyssa was so shaken,
her hands were trembling.

390
00:36:13,200 --> 00:36:14,480
She couldn't drive at all.

391
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:16,160
Then how did you get here?

392
00:36:17,480 --> 00:36:20,000
Mr. Rawee offered to drive us.

393
00:36:22,760 --> 00:36:24,000
Thank you, Rawee.

394
00:36:27,640 --> 00:36:28,840
And you get all the credit.

395
00:36:29,880 --> 00:36:32,160
Aunt Pat, if it weren't for him,

396
00:36:32,240 --> 00:36:35,160
you might've had to take a van,
or we could've crashed.

397
00:36:45,440 --> 00:36:50,440
Hey! You stressed your brother so badly
he ended up here, and you still show up?

398
00:36:50,520 --> 00:36:54,240
Whoa. Why are you blaming me?

399
00:36:54,320 --> 00:36:56,040
Nimit was already sick, wasn't he?

400
00:36:56,920 --> 00:36:58,600
I should be asking you

401
00:36:59,200 --> 00:37:00,120
how you've been taking care of him.

402
00:37:02,160 --> 00:37:03,960
Why are you here again?

403
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:07,800
We're not done talking.

404
00:37:09,600 --> 00:37:11,680
If you're not family,

405
00:37:11,760 --> 00:37:13,040
finish your visit and leave.

406
00:37:13,120 --> 00:37:15,200
Jak, don't be rude.

407
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:18,080
I don't need to be polite

408
00:37:18,800 --> 00:37:20,520
to a bunch of scammers.

409
00:37:21,720 --> 00:37:23,720
If there's a scammer in this room,

410
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:25,480
I'd say it's you, Uncle Jak.

411
00:37:26,840 --> 00:37:29,160
Hey. Watch your mouth.

412
00:37:29,240 --> 00:37:30,960
You're the one
who should watch your mouth.

413
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:32,160
Look.

414
00:37:32,240 --> 00:37:34,640
You've already made plenty off the resort.

415
00:37:34,720 --> 00:37:37,960
You've had more than enough,
and now you want to sell it too?

416
00:37:38,040 --> 00:37:39,400
Aren't you being a little greedy?

417
00:37:43,480 --> 00:37:45,680
What business is it of yours?

418
00:37:46,480 --> 00:37:48,200
This is between brothers.

419
00:37:49,040 --> 00:37:50,160
Oh.

420
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:51,520
Are you trying

421
00:37:51,600 --> 00:37:53,720
to take your sister's place as his wife?

422
00:37:53,800 --> 00:37:56,040
Hey! Get out.

423
00:37:58,920 --> 00:38:00,320
So what's it going to be?

424
00:38:00,400 --> 00:38:02,880
You won't sign off
on selling me the resort?

425
00:38:02,960 --> 00:38:05,280
-Well?
-Let Ms. Alyssa go.

426
00:38:09,600 --> 00:38:11,080
What the hell is it to you?

427
00:38:11,160 --> 00:38:12,320
What?

428
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:15,320
You looking to marry into money too?

429
00:38:18,080 --> 00:38:19,880
-Let's settle this. Answer me.
-Hey!

430
00:38:19,960 --> 00:38:21,520
-Let Alyssa go!
-Are you selling or not?

431
00:38:21,600 --> 00:38:23,080
-Let her go!
-Ow!

432
00:38:24,320 --> 00:38:26,240
-You bitch!
-Hey! Don't hurt Alyssa!

433
00:38:26,320 --> 00:38:28,240
-Let me go!
-Don't hurt her!

434
00:38:28,320 --> 00:38:30,520
-Let go!
-Hey! Stop!

435
00:38:30,600 --> 00:38:31,520
Stop, Jak!

436
00:38:31,600 --> 00:38:33,000
-Let go!
-That's enough!

437
00:38:33,080 --> 00:38:34,640
-Stop!
-Enough!

438
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:37,440
-Let me go!
-Drag him out!

439
00:38:37,520 --> 00:38:40,480
-That's enough!
-Get him out!

440
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:45,400
-Mr. Jak! Come here!
-Let me go!

441
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:50,000
Let me go! Let go!
Where are you taking me?

442
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:53,480
What are you going to do to me?

443
00:38:54,480 --> 00:38:55,960
Who told you Mr. Nimit was sick?

444
00:38:57,520 --> 00:38:59,000
So, does he really have cancer?

445
00:39:00,760 --> 00:39:02,720
Mr. Nimit said not to talk about it.

446
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:07,240
Fine, we won't talk about his illness.

447
00:39:08,160 --> 00:39:10,640
But the inheritance needs to be settled.

448
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:13,160
Otherwise, Alyssa will get everything.

449
00:39:13,840 --> 00:39:15,560
Your boss could die any--

450
00:39:19,280 --> 00:39:21,400
Unless you want to disappear
and turn up dead,

451
00:39:23,480 --> 00:39:25,120
go back to the island.

452
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:34,240
-Alyssa, are you okay?
-Wee, are you hurt?

453
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:39,000
Are you okay?

454
00:40:00,040 --> 00:40:03,480
Try paying as much attention to your work
as you are to your phone.

455
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:06,480
But the meeting's already over, Mom.

456
00:40:07,240 --> 00:40:08,760
The amount you withdrew

457
00:40:08,840 --> 00:40:12,160
doesn't match the expenses.
When will you get it sorted out?

458
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:15,800
I'll take care of it as soon as I can.

459
00:40:16,520 --> 00:40:18,480
I want an exact date and time.

460
00:40:19,760 --> 00:40:21,200
Come on, Mom.

461
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,800
This is my project.

462
00:40:22,880 --> 00:40:24,440
Give me some time.

463
00:40:24,520 --> 00:40:26,320
Everyone makes mistakes the first time.

464
00:40:27,080 --> 00:40:28,800
Make mistakes about anything you want,

465
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:31,840
but not the numbers in the accounts.

466
00:40:31,920 --> 00:40:34,160
If you're really focused on your work,

467
00:40:34,240 --> 00:40:36,760
why don't you know where the money went?

468
00:40:36,840 --> 00:40:39,000
Don't think having the upper hand

469
00:40:39,080 --> 00:40:40,680
means you can do whatever you want.

470
00:40:41,680 --> 00:40:43,520
If you try anything,

471
00:40:43,600 --> 00:40:45,160
I won't let you get away with it.

472
00:40:46,800 --> 00:40:48,200
Go ahead and try.

473
00:40:50,800 --> 00:40:52,120
Your secret

474
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:54,200
won't be a secret anymore.

475
00:40:56,840 --> 00:41:00,080
You don't even know who I really am.

476
00:41:07,760 --> 00:41:08,720
Think about it.

477
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:11,880
I've managed to hide
who I am for this long.

478
00:41:12,720 --> 00:41:14,120
Pretty good, aren't I?

479
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:18,280
And if I want to keep hiding it,
it won't be difficult.

480
00:41:19,080 --> 00:41:22,000
Don't forget, Rawee is still here.

481
00:41:22,720 --> 00:41:25,960
Proving who the rightful heir is
wouldn't be difficult.

482
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:30,000
Will you risk it?

483
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:34,200
I will. The question is, will you?

484
00:41:36,800 --> 00:41:38,600
Don't threaten me with this again.

485
00:41:39,360 --> 00:41:41,120
Just keep quiet and enjoy the money.

486
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:42,360
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">TMDNA Lab. How can I help you?</font></font></i>

487
00:42:43,200 --> 00:42:44,240
I have a question.

488
00:42:44,840 --> 00:42:47,080
If both parents have passed away,

489
00:42:47,160 --> 00:42:49,920
can DNA testing
still be done using other relatives?

490
00:42:51,400 --> 00:42:54,520
Like the maternal grandfather
or grandmother?

491
00:42:54,600 --> 00:42:55,800
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Yes.</font></font></i>

492
00:42:55,880 --> 00:42:57,240
Really?

493
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:58,240
Yes.

494
00:42:58,320 --> 00:43:01,320
We can do a DNA test
using the maternal grandparents.

495
00:43:01,400 --> 00:43:05,920
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But it's a little more complicated</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">than testing the parents.</font></font></i>

496
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:08,560
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">We would need DNA</font></font></i>

497
00:43:08,640 --> 00:43:10,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">from both the maternal grandfather</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">and grandmother,</font></font></i>

498
00:43:10,240 --> 00:43:11,640
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">because a grandchild</font></font></i>

499
00:43:11,720 --> 00:43:13,640
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">shares only about 25%</font></font></i>

500
00:43:13,720 --> 00:43:15,400
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">of their DNA with each one.</font></font></i>

501
00:43:16,160 --> 00:43:17,840
So that means

502
00:43:18,640 --> 00:43:21,800
if either grandparent has passed away,

503
00:43:22,800 --> 00:43:25,280
the results wouldn't be accurate, right?

504
00:43:25,360 --> 00:43:26,760
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">That's right.</font></font></i>

505
00:43:28,520 --> 00:43:32,040
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">But there are other ways we can test</font></font></i>

506
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:33,880
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">through the paternal grandparents.</font></font></i>

507
00:43:33,960 --> 00:43:37,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Are your paternal grandparents</font></font></i>
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">still alive?</font></font></i>

508
00:43:45,560 --> 00:43:47,440
RADIOLOGY DEPARTMENT

509
00:44:05,080 --> 00:44:07,040
You got hurt because of me again.

510
00:44:08,600 --> 00:44:09,960
Thank you so much.

511
00:44:11,760 --> 00:44:12,640
Oh.

512
00:44:13,520 --> 00:44:16,720
My dad called for you.
He would like to see you.

513
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:18,560
He has something to discuss with you.

514
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:20,800
What is it?

515
00:44:25,760 --> 00:44:26,920
Tell me right now.

516
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:29,240
What exactly is wrong with him?

517
00:44:30,320 --> 00:44:32,640
Just what Mr. Nimit told you.

518
00:44:33,280 --> 00:44:34,560
I don't believe it.

519
00:44:35,400 --> 00:44:37,440
His stomach pain doesn't seem normal.

520
00:44:37,520 --> 00:44:38,800
You're telling me

521
00:44:38,880 --> 00:44:42,120
it's lack of sleep or high blood pressure?

522
00:44:42,840 --> 00:44:44,960
What does that have to do
with stomach pain?

523
00:44:49,320 --> 00:44:51,920
Look, I won't tell Alyssa.

524
00:44:54,120 --> 00:44:56,200
Ms. Alyssa already knows everything.

525
00:44:58,520 --> 00:44:59,840
Alyssa already knows?

526
00:45:00,560 --> 00:45:02,800
Then what exactly is wrong with him?

527
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:10,680
Come on, tell me.
What does he really have?

528
00:45:14,640 --> 00:45:15,720
Colon cancer.

529
00:45:23,560 --> 00:45:24,600
And…

530
00:45:26,320 --> 00:45:27,680
What stage is it?

531
00:45:28,440 --> 00:45:29,760
Stage three.

532
00:45:32,840 --> 00:45:36,120
Take me to talk to his doctor.

533
00:45:37,840 --> 00:45:39,000
Sure.

534
00:45:53,480 --> 00:45:54,800
They're back.

535
00:45:59,640 --> 00:46:01,600
Does it hurt, dear?

536
00:46:02,480 --> 00:46:03,640
Just a little.

537
00:46:04,520 --> 00:46:07,640
Rawee, come closer.

538
00:46:12,840 --> 00:46:14,600
Can you take some time off work?

539
00:46:17,200 --> 00:46:18,560
I think so.

540
00:46:20,600 --> 00:46:22,160
I have a favor to ask.

541
00:46:23,520 --> 00:46:26,920
Please go to Tawan Island
and accompany Alyssa.

542
00:46:34,760 --> 00:46:38,160
Actually, I've already spoken
to Rawee about it.

543
00:46:38,760 --> 00:46:40,800
Since he studied law,

544
00:46:40,880 --> 00:46:42,840
I thought he could review the agreements.

545
00:46:46,400 --> 00:46:48,880
Mr. Nimit, have you had the resort
on Tawan Island for long?

546
00:46:50,560 --> 00:46:52,200
Twenty, 30 years or so.

547
00:46:53,920 --> 00:46:56,280
Then you must know
about Ms. Nada and her husband

548
00:46:56,360 --> 00:46:58,160
being attacked, right?

549
00:47:00,880 --> 00:47:03,760
Even now, I still don't know
who was behind it.

550
00:47:14,600 --> 00:47:16,000
Why do you want to know about that?

551
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:35,760
Korn.

552
00:47:36,640 --> 00:47:38,880
You had me invest another 20 million
from the company.

553
00:47:38,960 --> 00:47:40,600
And with the market down like this,

554
00:47:40,680 --> 00:47:42,120
how can I pay it back?

555
00:47:45,680 --> 00:47:47,160
Calm down, nephew.

556
00:47:49,320 --> 00:47:51,480
You know, when you invest in stocks,

557
00:47:52,440 --> 00:47:55,600
a dip is exactly when you should buy.

558
00:47:56,200 --> 00:47:57,560
Look at my portfolio.

559
00:47:58,400 --> 00:48:01,160
I've been buying the dip all day.
Loving it.

560
00:48:03,160 --> 00:48:05,760
Just buy the dip and wait.

561
00:48:06,480 --> 00:48:07,600
It'll go back up.

562
00:48:08,440 --> 00:48:09,680
But I can't wait.

563
00:48:09,760 --> 00:48:11,800
I need to pay the company back now.

564
00:48:24,440 --> 00:48:26,280
I heard you're using the Tayawat name now.

565
00:48:27,840 --> 00:48:29,040
Why get so worked up?

566
00:48:29,800 --> 00:48:32,000
Twenty million is nothing

567
00:48:33,200 --> 00:48:35,480
compared to the Tayawat inheritance.

568
00:48:38,040 --> 00:48:39,200
Don't stress about it.

569
00:48:40,200 --> 00:48:41,440
Take it easy.

570
00:48:42,400 --> 00:48:43,640
Trust me.

571
00:48:45,200 --> 00:48:46,360
Just calm down.

572
00:49:11,880 --> 00:49:13,680
We have the test results.

573
00:49:13,760 --> 00:49:17,400
The patient's abdominal cramps
are caused by colon cancer.

574
00:49:17,480 --> 00:49:19,040
PHAKORN

575
00:49:36,000 --> 00:49:38,920
PHAKORN

576
00:50:19,200 --> 00:50:21,280
I won't be able to help you close up, Mom.

577
00:50:21,360 --> 00:50:23,040
I have to return Ms. Alyssa's car first.

578
00:50:23,960 --> 00:50:25,160
That's okay.

579
00:50:25,240 --> 00:50:27,360
Are you heading back now
or staying the night?

580
00:50:28,160 --> 00:50:30,120
I'm going to talk to Ms. Nada first.

581
00:50:30,960 --> 00:50:34,640
If you can't reach me, don't worry.
My phone's dead.

582
00:50:35,760 --> 00:50:36,920
Okay.

583
00:50:37,560 --> 00:50:38,760
Wee.

584
00:50:39,440 --> 00:50:42,760
It'd be good if you stayed
with Mr. Nimit and Alyssa for now.

585
00:50:42,840 --> 00:50:45,400
Our family owes them a lot.

586
00:50:46,160 --> 00:50:47,560
Yes, Mom.

587
00:51:02,480 --> 00:51:04,760
-Alright.
-Let's go.

588
00:51:17,840 --> 00:51:18,920
Hello, Korn.

589
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:21,640
What's Wee doing in Chonburi, Mom?

590
00:51:22,600 --> 00:51:24,920
Wee drove Alyssa to see Mr. Nimit.

591
00:51:25,000 --> 00:51:27,680
He had to be rushed to the hospital.

592
00:51:28,280 --> 00:51:31,360
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">And Wee's phone is dead.</font></font></i>

593
00:51:31,440 --> 00:51:33,760
You couldn't reach him, could you?

594
00:52:30,080 --> 00:52:31,000
PHAKORN

595
00:52:39,400 --> 00:52:41,360
-Hello?
-Hey, Wee.

596
00:52:41,440 --> 00:52:43,040
Where are you? Who are you with?

597
00:52:43,120 --> 00:52:44,920
I'm at a hospital in Chonburi.

598
00:52:45,520 --> 00:52:46,680
I came to see Mr. Nimit.

599
00:52:47,280 --> 00:52:48,160
Who are you with?

600
00:52:49,240 --> 00:52:50,640
I'm alone right now.

601
00:52:51,600 --> 00:52:52,640
Is something wrong?

602
00:52:52,720 --> 00:52:55,560
Alyssa isn't answering my calls.
Are you with her?

603
00:52:56,960 --> 00:52:58,280
I just dropped Mom off.

604
00:52:59,200 --> 00:53:00,920
Ms. Alyssa is probably busy with work.

605
00:53:43,920 --> 00:53:45,360
If you need to cry, just cry.

606
00:53:46,040 --> 00:53:47,640
You don't have to be strong all the time.

607
00:53:53,680 --> 00:53:54,880
It's okay to be weak sometimes.

608
00:53:56,160 --> 00:53:58,560
Go ahead and cry. I won't make fun of you.

609
00:54:12,960 --> 00:54:14,320
You know,

610
00:54:15,600 --> 00:54:17,640
I really envy you and Korn.

611
00:54:19,040 --> 00:54:20,960
You have each other to lean on.

612
00:54:23,600 --> 00:54:25,080
I feel like

613
00:54:25,840 --> 00:54:27,160
I'm all alone.

614
00:54:27,680 --> 00:54:29,840
Like I have to fight everything by myself.

615
00:54:40,200 --> 00:54:41,480
Then just think of me…

616
00:54:43,520 --> 00:54:45,440
as a brother.

617
00:54:58,320 --> 00:55:01,640
Sometimes I wish I'd been born a man.

618
00:55:02,720 --> 00:55:04,240
Maybe I'd be stronger,

619
00:55:04,880 --> 00:55:06,960
and Dad wouldn't have to worry so much.

620
00:55:50,960 --> 00:55:52,000
Korn.

621
00:55:59,200 --> 00:56:01,280
Korn!

622
00:56:02,120 --> 00:56:03,480
Korn!

623
00:56:05,840 --> 00:56:08,280
You said you were alone.
Why did you lie to me?

624
00:56:08,360 --> 00:56:09,880
Just listen.

625
00:56:09,960 --> 00:56:11,520
I was alone at first.

626
00:56:11,600 --> 00:56:13,200
I only ran into Ms. Alyssa just now.

627
00:56:14,040 --> 00:56:15,040
Liar.

628
00:56:16,360 --> 00:56:17,600
Listen to me, Korn.

629
00:56:17,680 --> 00:56:19,960
Why would I lie to you?

630
00:56:20,040 --> 00:56:22,240
If you want to know, ask Ms. Alyssa.

631
00:56:24,960 --> 00:56:26,760
Korn!

632
00:56:27,520 --> 00:56:29,840
Enough! Stop it!

633
00:56:32,200 --> 00:56:34,360
What the hell is wrong with you?

634
00:56:35,600 --> 00:56:36,960
What the hell is wrong with you?

635
00:56:37,040 --> 00:56:39,800
You're my girlfriend,
and you're hugging my brother?

636
00:56:39,880 --> 00:56:41,600
She was upset and crying.

637
00:56:41,680 --> 00:56:43,240
I was just comforting her.

638
00:56:43,320 --> 00:56:45,080
Nothing else happened, Korn.

639
00:56:45,160 --> 00:56:46,480
Is that really all?

640
00:56:47,080 --> 00:56:50,280
That's all. Whether
you believe me or not is up to you.

641
00:56:52,080 --> 00:56:54,000
You keep pretending
you're on my side, Wee.

642
00:56:54,080 --> 00:56:56,320
But you're out to stab me in the back,
aren't you?

643
00:56:58,440 --> 00:57:01,600
Or are you jealous
that I have a better life?

644
00:57:04,400 --> 00:57:06,960
Why would I do that? When…

645
00:57:07,040 --> 00:57:08,560
When what?

646
00:57:09,520 --> 00:57:12,520
You know perfectly well
I'm not jealous of you.

647
00:57:31,600 --> 00:57:35,040
Mr. Panas reported to the board
that Phakorn embezzled 20 million.

648
00:57:36,240 --> 00:57:37,760
Where is Phakorn now?

649
00:57:38,960 --> 00:57:41,000
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">You need to tell me the truth.</font></font></i>

650
00:57:41,080 --> 00:57:42,240
Otherwise,

651
00:57:42,320 --> 00:57:44,320
no one here can help you.

652
00:57:44,400 --> 00:57:46,160
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">I respected you like family.</font></font></i>

653
00:57:46,240 --> 00:57:47,720
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">Why the hell did you do this?</font></font></i>

654
00:57:48,400 --> 00:57:50,320
You really are an idiot.

655
00:57:50,400 --> 00:57:52,480
Who'd consider someone
from a mistress's family one of us?

656
00:57:53,080 --> 00:57:54,840
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">So you've finally shown your true colors.</font></font></i>

657
00:57:54,920 --> 00:57:58,120
You and Pim are exactly alike.

658
00:57:58,200 --> 00:57:59,520
Damn you, Nada!

659
00:57:59,600 --> 00:58:00,600
Got a problem, Panas?

660
00:58:01,800 --> 00:58:04,840
Are you pretending not to know,
or do you really not know

661
00:58:04,920 --> 00:58:06,920
how I feel about Korn?

662
00:58:07,000 --> 00:58:08,920
What are you using
my brother for this time?

663
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:10,400
Maybe…

664
00:58:11,040 --> 00:58:14,080
<i><font size="16"><font face="Arial">To find Aunt Da's real son.</font></font></i>

665
00:58:16,680 --> 00:58:18,200
I'll take care of my girlfriend myself.
